From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 15:44:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/22] fix(scheduler): misfire grace and coalescing; per-user
 cleanup minute honoured; budget reset trusts its UTC trigger

Bug (B-34): AsyncIOScheduler() ran with APScheduler's 1-second
misfire_grace_time. After a leader hand-over, a paused container or a slow
loop, any cron whose instant had passed was skipped silently - the monthly
budget reset included. Bare cron triggers also fired in UTC while admins
configure server-local times.
Bug (B-9): job_user_media_cleanup ran only at minute 0 of each hour and
skipped when now.minute < cleanup_minute, so any cleanup_minute other than
0 never ran.
Bug (job_reset_budgets): reset_all_monthly_budgets returned 0 unless
utcnow().day == 1 - a run that fired minutes late, or on a server east of
UTC at local 00:05 on the 1st (still the 31st in UTC), did nothing.

Change: scheduler job_defaults misfire_grace_time=300, coalesce=True,
max_instances=1 and timezone=get_server_timezone(); budget_reset keeps an
explicit timezone=UTC because budget periods are month-of-UTC everywhere
else, and the day guard is gone; user_media_cleanup polls every 15 minutes
and user_media_cleanup_due(prefs, now) decides ("today's slot has passed
and last_cleanup_at is before it").

Tests: tests/test_scheduler_defaults.py.

